{"id": "unknown-2026-10-22-004", "date": "2026-10-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Aiko to convert PERC factory into 6 GW of ABC cell capacity", "content": "<p>The Chinese company says it will convert the manufacturing capacity at its base in Tianjin into its proprietary all-back-contact (ABC) technology as the efficiency of passivated emitter and rear contact (PERC) solar cells reaches “a bottleneck”.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/aiko-to-convert-perc-factory-into-6-gw-of-abc-cell-capacity/\">Aiko to convert PERC factory into 6 GW of ABC cell capacity</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv ma", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/aiko-to-convert-perc-factory-into-6-gw-of-abc-cell-capacity/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-22-005", "date": "2026-10-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["trade_tariff", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Iraq removes import tariffs on solar systems", "content": "<p>The measure coincides with the completion of a draft set of regulations set to govern the connection of solar energy systems to Iraq’s national grid.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/iraq-removes-import-tariffs-on-solar-systems/\">Iraq removes import tariffs on solar systems</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/iraq-removes-import-tariffs-on-solar-systems/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-22-006", "date": "2026-10-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Rwanda tenders 200 MW floating PV, 800 MWh BESS project", "content": "<p>A tender is open in Rwanda for a 200 MW floating solar plant to be tied to 800 MWh of battery storage. The deadline to submit pre-qualification bids is November 12.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/rwanda-tenders-200-mw-floating-pv-800-mwh-bess-project/\">Rwanda tenders 200 MW floating PV, 800 MWh BESS project</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/rwanda-tenders-200-mw-floating-pv-800-mwh-bess-project/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-22-007", "date": "2026-10-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Engie starts building first co-located solar and battery project in France", "content": "<p>Engie has begun construction of its first co-located solar and battery project in France, combining 29.8 MW of solar capacity with a 20 MWh battery system to shift electricity delivery to periods of higher grid demand.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/engie-starts-building-first-co-located-solar-and-battery-project-in-france/\">Engie starts building first co-located solar and battery project in France</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/engie-starts-building-first-co-located-solar-and-battery-project-in-france/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-22-008", "date": "2026-10-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar-assisted CO₂ heat pump achieves 18.7% COP increase as irradiance rises", "content": "<p>Researchers in Italy have tested a 10 kW dual-source heat pump using CO₂ as a refrigerant and air or photovoltaic-thermal collectors as heat sources. The results show that solar operation can improve heating performance under favorable irradiance conditions, while an optimized source-switching strategy delivers modest annual electricity savings.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/solar-assisted-co%e2%82%82-heat-pump-achieves-18-7-cop-increase-as-irradiance-rises/\"", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/solar-assisted-co%e2%82%82-heat-pump-achieves-18-7-cop-increase-as-irradiance-rises/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-22-009", "date": "2026-10-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Spanish region announce tax on ground mounted PV", "content": "<p>The Spanish region of Castilla y León plans to extend its environmental impact tax to ground-mounted solar installations from 2027. Spanish solar association UNEF has criticised the proposal, arguing that PV projects already face multiple taxes and that the new levy lacks environmental justification.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/spanish-region-announce-tax-on-ground-mounted-pv/\">Spanish region announce tax on ground mounted PV</a> appeared first on <a href=\"", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/spanish-region-announce-tax-on-ground-mounted-pv/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-22-010", "date": "2026-10-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Rio Tinto plans 360 MWh thermal battery for Australian alumina refinery", "content": "<p>Rio Tinto is assessing a 360 MWh thermal battery to replace fossil fuels in alumina refining, with the proposed Australian project potentially cutting annual emissions by 67,000 metric tons of carbon dioxide.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/rio-tinto-plans-360-mwh-thermal-battery-for-australian-alumina-refinery/\">Rio Tinto plans 360 MWh thermal battery for Australian alumina refinery</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/rio-tinto-plans-360-mwh-thermal-battery-for-australian-alumina-refinery/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-22-011", "date": "2026-10-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "UNSW researchers find east-west ground-mounted PV shows less degradation than single-axis tracking counterparts", "content": "<p>Researchers at the University of New South Wales found that east-west ground-mounted PV systems can experience up to 40% lower rates of certain degradation mechanisms than single-axis trackers. Their simulations showed that lower operating temperatures and reduced UV exposure could improve module reliability, particularly in remote installations.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/unsw-researchers-find-east-west-ground-mounted-pv-shows-less-degradation-than-single", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/unsw-researchers-find-east-west-ground-mounted-pv-shows-less-degradation-than-single-axis-tracking-counterparts/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "longi-2026-10-22-012", "date": "2026-10-22", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": ["longi"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "LONGi unveils intelligent manufacturing base in Suzhou to advance solar-storage integration", "content": "<p>The new base features upgraded manufacturing capabilities that reduce fault-related downtime losses by 75% and shorten the time needed to close quality issues by more than 50%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/longi-unveils-intelligent-manufacturing-base-in-suzhou-to-advance-solar-storage-integration/\">LONGi unveils intelligent manufacturing base in Suzhou to advance solar-storage integration</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazin", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/22/longi-unveils-intelligent-manufacturing-base-in-suzhou-to-advance-solar-storage-integration/", "type": "rss"}]}
